ple and the environment around you"},{"name":"A strong sense of well-being"}],"combinations":[{"substance":"Lithium","status":"Dangerous","tone":"danger","note":"Documented dangerous interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"Tramadol","status":"Unsafe","tone":"danger","note":"Documented unsafe interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"Cannabis","status":"Caution","tone":"warning","note":"Uncertain or unpredictable interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"Stimulants","status":"Caution","tone":"warning","note":"Uncertain or unpredictable interaction on PsychonautWiki."}],"citations":[],"helpfulLinks":[{"title":"PsychonautWiki","description":"Pharmacology, subjective effects, and dosage reference","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/AL-LAD"},{"title":"TripSit Factsheet","description":"Rapid harm-reduction summary and combination data","url":"https://drugs.tripsit.me/al-lad"},{"title":"Erowid Experience Vaults","description":"First-person experience reports and archives","url":"https://www.erowid.org/experiences/subs/exp_ALLAD.shtml"},{"title":"TiHKAL Entry","description":"Alexander & Ann Shulgin tryptamine monograph","url":"https://www.erowid.org/library/books_online/tihkal/tihkal01.shtml"},{"title":"Wikipedia","description":"Encyclopedia article","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AL-LAD"},{"title":"Wikidata","description":"Structured data on AL-LAD","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q4652233"}],"wikidata":"Q4652233","pharmacology":{"text":"AL-LAD has been found to interact with the serotonin 5-HT1 and 5-HT2 receptors and with the dopamine D1 and D2 receptors. It is known to act as a potent full agonist of the serotonin 5-HT2A receptor. The drug was about 3.5-fold more potent than LSD in substituting for LSD in drug discrimination tests in rodents. Conversely however, AL-LAD was similar in potency to LSD in humans.","source":"Wikipedia","page":"AL-LAD","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AL-LAD#Pharmacodynamics","kind":"Non-selective serotonin receptor agonist; Serotonin 5-HT2A receptor agonist; Serotonergic psychedelic; Hallucinogen","figures":"AL-LAD"},"uses":{"text":"AL-LAD was encountered as a novel designer recreational drug by 2015. The related drugs 1P-AL-LAD, 1cP-AL-LAD, and 1T-AL-LAD are thought to function as prodrugs of AL-LAD and have also been encountered as designer drugs in the 2020s.","source":"Wikipedia","page":"AL-LAD","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AL-LAD","routes":"Oral","figures":"AL-LAD"}}